# No hardcoded user-facing text

All user-facing text must come from translation files in `src/messages/` through `next-intl`.

## Rule

- Do **not** hardcode visible UI text in components, screens, layouts, hooks, modals, toasts, validation messages, placeholders, button labels, headings, helper text, or empty states.
- Use `useTranslations("<namespace>")` in client components and `getTranslations("<namespace>")` in server code.
- Keep text as i18n keys in `src/messages/<locale>/*.json` (`en`, `ar`, `es`, `fr`) and reference them in code.
- Prefer existing namespaces (`auth`, `common`, `home`) and add new keys in all locales when needed.

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
const t = useTranslations("common");
<Button>{t("save")}</Button>
<Input placeholder={t("searchPlaceholder")} />

// ❌ BAD
<Button>Save</Button>
<Input placeholder="Search..." />
```

## Validation and errors

- Validation messages must use translation keys (not hardcoded strings).
- Toast titles/descriptions and modal copy must use translation keys.
- Fallback text should also be localized.

## Notes

- Internal-only identifiers are fine to keep as literals (e.g., object keys, enum values, route segments, API fields, test IDs).
- This rule applies to **user-visible** text only.
